==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|la|circulatus}}, past participle of {{der|en|LL.|circulo|circulare|make circular, encircle}}, a later collateral form of {{m|la|circulari||form a circle (of men) around oneself}}, from {{m|la|circulus||a circle}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|sər'kü-lāt}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈsɚ.kjʊˌleɪt/}}
* {{audio|en|En-us-circulate.ogg|a=US}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} to [[move]] in [[circle]]s or through a [[circuit]]
# {{lb|en|transitive}} to cause (a person or thing) to move in [[circle]]s or through a [[circuit]]
# to move from [[person]] to person, as at a [[party]]
# to [[spread]] or [[disseminate]]
#: ''to '''circulate''' money or gossip''
# to become [[widely]] [[known]]
# {{lb|en|math}} Of [[decimal]]s: to [[repeat]].

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|put about}}
* {{l|en|spread}}
* {{l|en|disseminate}}

